.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH gpuq-desktop 1  "gpuq 0.3.1" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
gpuq\-desktop \- Show or change what gpuq does with the desktop ([desktop] in the config)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgpuq desktop\fR [\fB\-\-api\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show or change what gpuq does with the desktop ([desktop] in the config)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-api\fR \fI<HOST:PORT>\fR
Address of the gpuq control API (default: $GPUQ_API, else 127.0.0.1:9390)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
gpuq\-desktop\-status(1)
Show the state, why, and the processes on the card (the default)
.TP
gpuq\-desktop\-release(1)
Free the card now: move or stop the desktop as the policy says
.TP
gpuq\-desktop\-restore(1)
Give the desktop back now, and hold off automatic releases
.TP
gpuq\-desktop\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgpuq\fR(1)
